        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Victor Garber, Teri Copley, Lloyd Bridges, Aaron Spelling, James Cameron, Ken Taylor\n- Television series: I Had Three Wives, We Got It Made, The Lloyd Bridges Show, Alias\n- Films and stage works: Godspell, Assassins, Lend Me a Tenor, Titanic, Argo\n- Roles: Jesus, Anthony Hope, John Wilkes Booth, Jack Bristow, Max, Thomas Andrews, Canadian Ambassador to Iran\n\nFacts:\n- The Lloyd Bridges Show was an American anthology drama series produced by Aaron Spelling that aired on CBS from September 11, 1962 to May 28, 1963.\n- The Lloyd Bridges Show starred and was hosted by Lloyd Bridges.\n- We Got It Made premiered in 1983 as an American NBC/syndicated television series.\n- Teri Copley was known for a role on We Got It Made.\n- In 1985, Teri Copley co-starred on the CBS television series I Had Three Wives.\n- Victor Garber had his first starring role on television as the lead of I Had Three Wives.\n- Victor Garber is known for playing Jesus in Godspell, Anthony Hope in an unspecified work, John Wilkes Booth in Assassins, Jack Bristow in Alias, Max in Lend Me a Tenor, Thomas Andrews in James Cameron's Titanic, and Ken Taylor in Argo.",
